  "content": {
    "id": "p90-q40-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $y=\\dfrac{ax+b}{cx+d}$, where $a,b,c,d\\ne0$. Find the:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p90-q40-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x$-intercept.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p90-q40-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "ad\\ne bc",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ": ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\left(-\\frac{b}{a},0\\right)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "ad=bc",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ": no ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "-intercept.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p90-q40-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Set the numerator to zero and check that the denominator is nonzero.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For an $x$-intercept, $y=0$ and the denominator must be nonzero.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}ax+b&=0\\\\x&=-\\frac{b}{a}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt this candidate,\n\n$$c\\left(-\\frac{b}{a}\\right)+d=\\frac{ad-bc}{a}.$$\n\nIf $ad\\ne bc$, the denominator is nonzero, so the $x$-intercept is $\\left(-\\frac{b}{a},0\\right)$.\n\nIf $ad=bc$, the only zero of the numerator is an excluded input. There is no $x$-intercept.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p90-q40-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y$-intercept.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(0,\\dfrac{b}{d}\\right)$.",
          "worked": "Set $x=0$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{a(0)+b}{c(0)+d}\\\\y&=\\frac{b}{d}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $d\\ne0$, the $y$-intercept is $\\left(0,\\frac{b}{d}\\right)$ in both cases.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p90-q40-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "vertical asymptote.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p90-q40-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "ad\\ne bc",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ": ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x=-\\frac{d}{c}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "ad=bc",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ": no vertical asymptote.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p90-q40-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Check for cancellation before treating a denominator zero as a vertical asymptote.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Set the denominator to zero:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}cx+d&=0\\\\x&=-\\frac{d}{c}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt this value, the numerator is\n\n$$a\\left(-\\frac{d}{c}\\right)+b=\\frac{bc-ad}{c}.$$\n\nIf $ad\\ne bc$, this is nonzero, so the vertical asymptote is $x=-\\frac{d}{c}$.\n\nIf $ad=bc$, then $b=\\frac{ad}{c}$ and\n\n$$\\begin{align*}ax+b&=ax+\\frac{ad}{c}\\\\ax+b&=\\frac{a}{c}(cx+d).\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $y=\\frac{a}{c}$ for $x\\ne-\\frac{d}{c}$. The graph has a hole at $\\left(-\\frac{d}{c},\\frac{a}{c}\\right)$ and no vertical asymptote.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p90-q40-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "horizontal asymptote.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p90-q40-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=\\frac{a}{c}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " is the horizontal limiting line in both cases.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p90-q40-d-short-qualification",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "If ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "ad=bc",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", the graph itself lies on this line, with ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x=-\\frac{d}{c}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " excluded.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For nonzero $x$, divide the numerator and denominator by $x$:\n\n$$y=\\frac{a+b/x}{c+d/x}.$$\n\nAs $x\\to\\pm\\infty$, both $\\frac{b}{x}$ and $\\frac{d}{x}$ approach zero, so $y\\to\\frac{a}{c}$.\n\nThe horizontal limiting line is $y=\\frac{a}{c}$. If $ad\\ne bc$, this is the hyperbola's horizontal asymptote. If $ad=bc$, the graph is the constant line $y=\\frac{a}{c}$ with $x=-\\frac{d}{c}$ excluded.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      }
    ]
  },
